Body:
A more simpler workaround for` opencode.json:`


```
"lsp": {
    "jdtls": {
      "command": [
        "jdtls"
      ],
      "env": {
        "JAVA_TOOL_OPTIONS": "-javaagent:c:/Users/<user-profile>/.opencode_addon/lombok.jar"
      }
    }
  }
```

^ For Bedrock users, the `headers` approach above doesn't exactly work. Bedrock requires anthropic beta headers to be included in the request body of their Converse API.

Instead, you can use `options` with `anthropicBeta`. Internally it gets translated into `additionalModelRequestFields.anthropic_beta` in the Converse API request body.

```json
{
  "provider": {
    "amazon-bedrock": {
      "models": {
        "us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-6-v1": {
          "limit": {
            "context": 1000000,
            "output": 128000
          },
          "options": {
            "anthropicBeta": ["context-1m-2025-08-07"]
          }
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

sdk 1.2.15 opencode 1.2.15 Windows


```
export async function ABORT(req: Request) {
  try {
    const {sessionId} = await req.json();

    if (sessionId) {
      await opencodeService.abort(sessionId);
      return new Response(JSON.stringify({success: true}), {
        status: 200,
        headers: {"Content-Type": "application/json"}
      });
    }
    return new Response(JSON.stringify({error: "SessionId required"}), {status: 400});
  } catch (error) {
    console.error("Abort Error:", error);
    return new Response(JSON.stringify({error: "Internal Abort Error"}), {status: 500});
  }
}
```
